	title="Meditation Practice"
	description="Meditation practice — groups, a library of guided recordings, and a Buddhist approach to presence."
>
	<p>For thousands of years, across many spiritual traditions, people have sat in simple, present-moment awareness.</p>
	<p>
		Meditation is a simple practice, though not always an easy one — a commitment to sit for a set
		period and observe without judgment or reaction.
	</p>
	<p>
		Sitting with a group and a guide brings real advantages: it strengthens commitment and makes it
		possible to work through difficulties through shared conversation.
	</p>
	<p><strong>Sangha</strong> — a group of people practicing together and supporting one another through learning and growth.</p>
	<h2>On this page</h2>
	<ul>
		<li>A library of guided meditation recordings (limited access — see note below)</li>
		<li>Two active meditation groups — in Tel Aviv and in Moshav Tal Shahar</li>
	</ul>
	<p class="note">
		<em
			>Note: the recordings library is still being rebuilt on the new site. On the previous site it
			was password-protected with no clear structure — it will be reorganized by practice type
			(breath awareness, body scan, compassion, Zen-style sitting), with a duration and description
			for each recording.</em
		>
	</p>
</ProsePage>

